  "body": "A conical hole (true angle 5.194 deg) is refused at 5.194 and 5.2 deg: \"wire gouge: the kerf of move 2 enters the part by 0.0019 mm ... (65 move(s) gouge)\". Top and bottom edges are meshed differently (64 vs 128 segments). 5.17 deg passes but leaves the bottom about 0.008 mm undersize, and verify says nothing: there is no undercut check for wire. The taper angle is also typed by hand; it cannot be read from the model wall.\n\nDone means: the gouge check judges the true cone (or a tolerance tied to the chord error) so the true angle passes; verify reports an undercut beyond tolerance; optional: read the taper angle from a picked wall.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
